## Linked issue

Follow-up to the upstream sync (#42). Fixes the failing check "Team API and reverse actions E2E".

## Type of change

- [x] Bug fix

## What changed

- Message batching no longer adds queued messages to a run-now turn (`src/backend/mailbox-store.ts`).
- A usage limit with no reported scope holds only the refused model, not the whole provider account (`usage-limit-gate.ts`, `turn-lifecycle.ts`, `claude-client.ts`, `agent-service.ts`).

Surfaces: backend agent runtime. No IPC, Team API wire, or migration change.

## Verification

- [ ] `test:backup-model-failover` and the steer/interrupt/pause step: the executor sandbox cannot start the fake provider CLIs, so CI is the first run.
- [x] `typecheck:node`, `test:team-legacy-clients`, Biome on changed files passed.
- [x] The pre-commit hook passed.

## Risk and security impact

Scope of a usage-limit hold is narrower. An explicit account-wide or family limit still holds as before.

Model and harness: Codex gpt-6.1-terra through openswarm; planner Claude Code.
